  "refinements": [
    "Corrected earlier precommit receipt wording and payload view: RootTransferPermit prepares a protected cut, RootTransferReceipt follows membership and target root publication",
    "Actual kernel save/reload, still allocation GC, direct resize GC, sync dispatch, RC cell writers and all collector phases require one complete admission law",
    "Strong-worker count or barrier return does not establish weak/continuation/cleanup/resize terminality, cached borrower drain or target root discovery",
    "Chosen stable same-VM/heap protocol holds terminal-epoch boundary across exact manifest construction, C membership mutation and G root/receipt publication; no rewrite of sealed ticket",
    "Cancellation versus Committing is serialized; stable C disposition publication precedes G consumption, and post-membership failure keeps target/prepared-root/VM/facility/work custody held",
    "Runtime coordinator in either C or Zig is the issuer; copied structs, compiler/statepoint artifacts or receipt history alone grant no current ownership or free authority",
    "ClosingTransfers preserves GC needed by existing users, then admits a successor same-heap route or resolves future heap use before closing old collector entry",
    "Old facility destruction additionally drains all scanners, queue users, cursors, waiters/signallers, transfer and resolution users; live heap lifetime is separate from particular mutex/epoch lifetime",
    "Native-only no-managed-reference profiles can make root transfer NotRequired but retain list/scanner/cleanup custody obligations; no blanket pause-free migration is established",
    "Nine support obligations, five maintenance events, symbolic pause/storage costs and five net conditions credit current C support and shared LLVM artifacts; no positive net bound"
  ],
